From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:57:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 092/138] ASoC: codecs: cs42l67: Program the serial port sample
 rate
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

iOS' enableAudio sets register 0x012 [3:0] to the stream rate code
(0x…86eeb58: 8k=1 ... 44.1k=8, 48k=9), the same codes as the CS42L73's
VXSPFS XSP field, where 0 means "unknown". We never wrote it, so the
codec ran with rate 0. Set 48 kHz on power-up, in the place iOS does.

This alone does not make capture work (tested live: SDOUT stays low),
but it matches iOS.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 sound/soc/codecs/cs42l67.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l67.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l67.c
index 7440f5915..d9567a8af 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l67.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs42l67.c
@@ -44,6 +44,9 @@
 #define  PATH_PDN_OUT		BIT(7)
 #define  PATH_PDN_IN		BIT(6)
 #define CS42L67_XSP_CFG1	0x011
+#define CS42L67_SP_FS		0x012	/* [3:0] serial port rate, CS42L73 VXSPFS codes */
+#define  SP_FS_MASK		GENMASK(3, 0)
+#define  SP_FS_48K		9	/* 8k=1 11.025k=2 12k=3 16k=4 22.05k=5 24k=6 32k=7 44.1k=8 */
 #define CS42L67_XSP_CTL		0x013
 #define  XSP_PDN		BIT(7)
 #define  XSP_TX_PDN		BIT(6)	/* codec -> AP */
@@ -243,6 +246,8 @@ static int cs42l67_power_up(struct cs42l67 *cs)
 	regmap_write(map, CS42L67_ANA_202, 0x00);
 	regmap_write(map, CS42L67_ANA_239, 0x00);
 	regmap_update_bits(map, CS42L67_OUT_CTL, 0x20, 0x20);
+	/* iOS sets the rate here (0x…86eeb58); 0 = "unknown" on the CS42L73 */
+	regmap_update_bits(map, CS42L67_SP_FS, SP_FS_MASK, SP_FS_48K);
 	regmap_write(map, CS42L67_MISC_130, 0xa0);
 
 	/*
